# High-tier paths: a PR touching any of these needs an approving review from a member of
# @qrtl/high-risk-reviewers who did not write it, before GitHub lets it merge. Everything
# else merges on green CI. Policy: qrtl-handbook-private, engineering/pr-risk-tiers.md.
# .github/ is owned, so a new or renamed workflow (a deploy.yml, say) is High by default.
# The files the OCA template generates are then released again: a later pattern with no
# owner leaves them unowned, so a copier update merges on green. What those files run is
# not guarded by the required checks (a job can keep its name and lose its steps), so a
# hand edit to them that is not a copier update gets a look before merging.
/.github/                              @qrtl/high-risk-reviewers
/.github/workflows/pre-commit.yml
/.github/workflows/test.yml
/.github/workflows/stale.yml
**/security/         @qrtl/high-risk-reviewers
**/migrations/       @qrtl/high-risk-reviewers
/account_*/          @qrtl/high-risk-reviewers
/stock_account*/     @qrtl/high-risk-reviewers
/stock_valuation*/   @qrtl/high-risk-reviewers
/*payment*/          @qrtl/high-risk-reviewers
/*payroll*/          @qrtl/high-risk-reviewers
/*tax*/              @qrtl/high-risk-reviewers
